<BaseLayout title="Contact — Freighthub" description="How to contact the Freighthub editorial desk: corrections, research questions and republication requests.">
  <article>
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <p class="article-meta">Editorial desk · Last reviewed 11 November 2026</p>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p><strong>editorial@freighthub.net</strong></p>
    <p>The address is monitored by the editorial desk. It is the right channel for corrections and factual challenges, source suggestions, questions about a page's reasoning, and permission requests for republishing.</p>

    <h2>What we can help with</h2>
    <p>We can point you to the page that covers a topic, explain the reasoning behind a judgement, and correct a factual error. We can also tell you when a question is outside the site's scope.</p>

    <h2>What we cannot do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>We cannot quote a freight rate.</strong> We are not a forwarder and do not have live carrier pricing.</li>
      <li><strong>We cannot clear a shipment.</strong> We are not a customs broker.</li>
      <li><strong>We cannot give legal, tax or investment advice.</strong> The pages are editorial analysis; the decisions remain yours.</li>
      <li><strong>We cannot recommend a specific forwarder or broker.</strong> We do not take commissions or referral fees.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Response times</h2>
    <p>We aim to acknowledge within five working days. Correction reports are prioritised. Research questions are answered when they fit the editorial calendar; not every question gets a custom reply.</p>

    <h2>Before you write</h2>
    <p>Check the <a href="/corrections/">corrections policy</a> and the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>. If your question is about a specific number, include the page URL and the sentence. It makes the response faster and more useful.</p>

    <h2>Postal and company details</h2>
    <p>Freighthub is an independent editorial project. It does not have a public office address or a company registration to publish at this stage. If that changes, it will be added here rather than invented.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
